     It's not necessary to see the scoreboard every time you die... with the
PC version, set your nethack.cnf with an options line like...
     ...(Greg thinks intently but can't remember the name of the option)...
     ...(Greg is saved by his comm program's view file function)...
options=endgame:own
     And it will only show you your own score.
     With Unix, use:
setenv NETHACKOPTIONS=endgame:own
     (Naturally, if you've already got some NETHACKOPTIONS, you'll have to
put in a comma.)
     The format for the endgame option is:
endgame:[x top/][x around/][own]
     At least, that's how I understand it.  Dunno what a blank endgames:
option would do; might skip the scorelist altogether, might turn out an
illegal options error when running the file.
     I usually use:
engame:5 top/5 around/own
     but for no particular reason.
     (Well, lately, I don't use anything at all, since I'm using the PC
version and I'm the sole resident of the high-score list.)
